[{:db/id "q-152926/selection/f3b3382e7adf0a31ef22e1825c0348c927e6dddd81b47330014b7ee1f62158b1" :answer/id #uuid "13b8bdcd-e562-5896-8852-2bea96cc4b7d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152926/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "cbd22ea0-a827-5c8a-806c-db2f6166d818" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152926/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2738eccb-b44f-5b91-82ea-d1ce45f3a82b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152926/selection/68ee7990c679da4221e974bf737d4c65351e6315adbede6c3f8bf610a59bde12" :answer/id #uuid "edf211b8-ec9b-5205-9c5f-22028b8914e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152926/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "634b81a7-35cd-52ff-8d08-b5ab88d80490" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152926/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03c42f49-eca4-548e-ba2a-946523e99270" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152926/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-152926/selection/f3b3382e7adf0a31ef22e1825c0348c927e6dddd81b47330014b7ee1f62158b1" "q-152926/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-152926/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-152926/selection/68ee7990c679da4221e974bf737d4c65351e6315adbede6c3f8bf610a59bde12" "q-152926/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152926" :question/id #uuid "9fb59805-3754-53e9-acab-d2034fbd41f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-152926" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x, & x<0 \\\\ 1, & x=0 \\\\ 3x, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=f(0)$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the middle branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(0)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=1.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(2x) \\\\  & =2(0) \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}(3x) \\\\  & =3(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=0\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=0\\ne f(0).$  $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since not all statements I-III are true, according to the continuity test, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152926/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152926"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-152832"] :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the second branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(1)=2-(1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=1.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(2x-1) \\\\  & =2(1)-1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(2-x) \\\\  & =2-(1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=1$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=1\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=1=f(1).$  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since all statements I-III are true, according to the continuity test, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-152925/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "969c0fdb-6009-571c-bc7c-ff6b76f9be86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152925/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "e9575c37-fc5a-56f8-a3de-9f9f695dc702" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152925/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f3a76e25-b0bc-540a-ac1b-bf188ebde065" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152925/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "3880a286-8228-5cfd-b329-e68bf6ce00f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152925/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "71f0083b-da14-55ab-8683-9d1e2f675e01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152925/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c89d7f1e-f33c-53c7-b62c-1fa840e86298" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152925/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-152925/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-152925/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-152925/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-152925/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" "q-152925/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152925" :question/id #uuid "ca3f1027-fa37-5b41-836a-b53bef56e3f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-152925" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3-x}, & x\\le -1 \\\\ x+1, & x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)$ exists\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the first branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(-1)=\\sqrt{3-(-1)}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is false. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}(\\sqrt{3-x}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3-(-1)} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}(x+1) \\\\  & =(-1)+1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=-1$ does not exist. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is false since the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=-1$ does not exist. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since not all statements I-III are true, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152925/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152925"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152913/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "50c95dc1-e2c5-58bf-b925-b2ff8e1cb413" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152913/selection/b37d32edd92c5a2b44069c29e35844b5f1ed599f01225cff80557800733db261" :answer/id #uuid "73db96e1-0290-52c5-8e94-5d9ae0305525" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152913/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "34f6fbdd-23e1-52b8-b625-2c7487c9e0b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152913/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7f97b4f3-95fb-5c86-953f-c94d45f6c58a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152913/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "857c034e-d0fc-5b89-9f87-4dc07af174d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152913/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "517f5a4a-d694-5d8e-a834-0fda70aee1b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152913/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-152913/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" "q-152913/selection/b37d32edd92c5a2b44069c29e35844b5f1ed599f01225cff80557800733db261" "q-152913/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-152913/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-152913/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152913" :question/id #uuid "86e8b7b9-d7d8-5f9b-a33a-a4700cd37236" :question/math-academy-id "q-152913" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x<0 \\\\ 0, & x=0 \\\\ {e}^{-x}, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=f(0)$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the middle branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(x+1) \\\\  & =(0)+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=1\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=1\\ne f(0).$  $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since not all statements I-III are true, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152913/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152913"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152930/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1ee093d1-d3c3-5215-8ebb-784938c84622" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152930/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "c356702c-14be-5c6d-88f3-b0c32c676e80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152930/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "865f9605-d157-562c-a78e-7e32f332ca7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152930/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a8f643b9-9b4d-5170-af69-54725ce4eda2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152930/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "235dbeb3-10ba-5180-b565-3def804f73e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152930/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee64c490-5138-5fc7-9f6b-9c529d9ee604" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152930/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer-field/choices ["q-152930/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-152930/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" "q-152930/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-152930/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-152930/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152930" :question/id #uuid "ee5d233d-2aed-58d4-99ac-cdfc6dfd9b29" :question/math-academy-id "q-152930" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-4-x, & x\\le 2 \\\\ -3x, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=f(2)$\n- $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the first branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(2)=-4-2=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(-4-x) \\\\  & =-4-2 \\\\  & =-6 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(-3x) \\\\  & =-3(2) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-6\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-6=f(2).$  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since all statements I-III are true, according to the continuity test, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-152930/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152930"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71076/selection/26b55b1efc3915ba4297376c78457707fc2c6f3468227cc31a23afb328e36aae" :answer/id #uuid "9210bb2e-25c9-503d-90b5-a33ac4060c04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71076/selection/5306f82049c45ad3a17e1ed88a928028b290b9edae55a6d3340e6f7ec897c56b" :answer/id #uuid "cc2c608a-ea05-5386-ab76-4d83fbbf7f0a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71076/selection/96dc30325f6b16a436759bdd3f21f4077751b2bf01c97d882e90dff7341d45bf" :answer/id #uuid "75975b3d-de90-593a-95c7-2354c820919f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-2)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71076/selection/43ca6c5914f91d8f31b8738564b86d90ece753f0744ce672e68528d81c49bfa9" :answer/id #uuid "af7feb0c-b8e0-554c-9dc9-d4ab75167d28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71076/selection/8d9f1a5499959514d0130e61b7e362542197494ce49e0fa494fdfbabbacccb7f" :answer/id #uuid "4064667e-f318-5813-8896-441bce75fe93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)\\ne f(-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71076/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd4f224f-2e33-5d47-83fd-523e2158759b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71076/selection/8d9f1a5499959514d0130e61b7e362542197494ce49e0fa494fdfbabbacccb7f" :answer-field/choices ["q-71076/selection/26b55b1efc3915ba4297376c78457707fc2c6f3468227cc31a23afb328e36aae" "q-71076/selection/5306f82049c45ad3a17e1ed88a928028b290b9edae55a6d3340e6f7ec897c56b" "q-71076/selection/96dc30325f6b16a436759bdd3f21f4077751b2bf01c97d882e90dff7341d45bf" "q-71076/selection/43ca6c5914f91d8f31b8738564b86d90ece753f0744ce672e68528d81c49bfa9" "q-71076/selection/8d9f1a5499959514d0130e61b7e362542197494ce49e0fa494fdfbabbacccb7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71076" :question/id #uuid "bc0af586-1383-50ca-8658-5c40cee85c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-71076" :question/problem "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ given below have a discontinuity at $x=-2?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-x, & x<-2 \\\\ 6, & x=-2 \\\\ -{x}^{2}+x, & x>-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-2.$\n\n- $f(-2)=6,$ so $f(-2)$ exists. $✓$\n\n- We calculate the one-sided limits and check if they coincide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}({x}^{3}-x) \\\\  & =(-2)^{3}-(-2) \\\\  & =-8+2 \\\\  & =-6, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}(-{x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =-(-2)^{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =-4-2 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)=-6$ $✓$\n\n- The limit of the function is not equal to the function value: ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)=-6,$ while $f(-2)=6.$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-2$ because ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)\\ne f(-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71076/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa1ddb40-3494-541c-b23e-b15dd98bf669"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104132/selection/0cac882e457c016c9f314d89919ca330b220195498ef1b880515bf5adc44351b" :answer/id #uuid "5a067ae2-a66a-54fe-8208-9057f295963b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is a piecewise function" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104132/selection/8d9f1a5499959514d0130e61b7e362542197494ce49e0fa494fdfbabbacccb7f" :answer/id #uuid "681f4311-729c-592e-a175-9c145b03dae0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)\\ne f(-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104132/selection/43ca6c5914f91d8f31b8738564b86d90ece753f0744ce672e68528d81c49bfa9" :answer/id #uuid "6ef08972-33aa-5845-bc2b-4cdc882f0d73" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104132/selection/96dc30325f6b16a436759bdd3f21f4077751b2bf01c97d882e90dff7341d45bf" :answer/id #uuid "a36646ee-7402-56ef-9b63-9227a45b7f1d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-2)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104132/selection/5306f82049c45ad3a17e1ed88a928028b290b9edae55a6d3340e6f7ec897c56b" :answer/id #uuid "ee63c00c-1971-57b2-8a48-1536c895ecb5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104132/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "298c38df-1b7a-559b-8f9a-3c1a64c60bf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104132/selection/8d9f1a5499959514d0130e61b7e362542197494ce49e0fa494fdfbabbacccb7f" :answer-field/choices ["q-104132/selection/0cac882e457c016c9f314d89919ca330b220195498ef1b880515bf5adc44351b" "q-104132/selection/8d9f1a5499959514d0130e61b7e362542197494ce49e0fa494fdfbabbacccb7f" "q-104132/selection/43ca6c5914f91d8f31b8738564b86d90ece753f0744ce672e68528d81c49bfa9" "q-104132/selection/96dc30325f6b16a436759bdd3f21f4077751b2bf01c97d882e90dff7341d45bf" "q-104132/selection/5306f82049c45ad3a17e1ed88a928028b290b9edae55a6d3340e6f7ec897c56b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104132" :question/id #uuid "7cf2bc26-58b9-5c11-9e2f-19000ce8d101" :question/math-academy-id "q-104132" :question/problem "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ below have a discontinuity at $x=-2?$ \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{2}, & x<-2 \\\\ 5, & x=-2 \\\\ \\frac{18}{{x}^{2}+2}, & x>-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-2.$\n\n- $f(-2)=5,$ so $f(-2)$ exists. $✓$\n\n- We calculate the one-sided limits and find that they coincide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)^{2}+2}{2} \\\\  & =3, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}(\\frac{18}{{x}^{2}+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{(-2)^{2}+2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)=3.\\,\\,✓$ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\n- The limit of the function is not equal to the function value: ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)=3,$ while $f(-2)=5.$ $\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-2$ because ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)\\ne f(-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa1ddb40-3494-541c-b23e-b15dd9